# The both-directions evidence that backs a VERDICT tier and lives outside this repository's own
# test sources.
#
# TrustTier.VERDICT means a finding says the code is wrong, so promotion to it requires a case that
# fires on a bug and a case that stays silent on the correct twin. DetectorTrustCoverageTest
# resolves that evidence by reflection, which reaches only test methods in this module. The corpus
# eval holds pairs of exactly the same shape on unmodified third-party code, in a downstream module
# no test here can see: this file is how the two halves reach each other.
#
# Each line names a detector and its pair, as
#
#   DETECTOR_TYPE = fires-on-the-bug, stays-silent-on-the-twin
#
# and both sides check it. In this module, DetectorTrustCoverageTest requires every VERDICT row to
# be backed either by a pair of test methods it can resolve or by a line here, and requires every
# line here to name a detector actually classified VERDICT. In corpus-eval, CorpusGates requires
# each named id to be a RecordingSubject for that detector carrying that expectation, so a line
# that stops being true fails the corpus build rather than quietly vouching for a tier.
#
# The bar is the one the in-repo pairs meet: the two subjects differ in the defect and in nothing
# else. The detectors on a "# held: TYPE" line below are corpus-measured and deliberately absent,
# and the reason in each case is the detector's model rather than the pair (#406, #419).
# DetectorTrustCoverageTest refuses a held detector that is also registered here or classified
# VERDICT, and so a commented-out registration kept with the class that capped it, as in the last
# section: the argument and the tier cannot disagree again (#818). Whether the argument still
# describes the detector is a reading, and no gate does that.
#
# held: CACHE_CONCURRENCY
#   CACHE_CONCURRENCY asks the map's own type whether it synchronizes itself, so given one class
#   both halves of a pair get the same answer by construction and no same-class pair can exist. It
#   also consults no lock at all, so a HashMap correctly guarded by the caller's own lock draws the
#   same finding as a raced one. That is the definition of PROMPT.
#
# FILE_CHANNEL_POSITION_RACE was held here from #755 until 2026-09-26, when #819 made the detector
# judge the seek-then-I/O sequence rather than single accesses; it is registered below, and its
# line says how.
#
#   CONCURRENT_MAP_CHECK_THEN_ACT was held here from 2026-08-29 because its only decision was
#   whether more than one thread reached the same (map, key): recordCheckThenAct is the body saying
#   a check-then-act happened, so a finding said no more than the body had. Re-asked on 2026-09-26
#   (#818), and it no longer holds. Since 2026-09-25 the detector keeps SelfGuard's per-round
#   lockset and happens-before model, so a check-then-act that every caller makes inside one lock,
#   the map's own monitor, a lock declared through HeldLocks or one the agent wove, stays silent,
#   and so does one ordered after another's. The recorded call now names an operation that is
#   correct on one thread, under one lock or in order, not the defect; the finding is the
#   detector's own: two callers on one key, unordered, with no lock in common. That is CONTEXTUAL,
#   the same evidence the Shared* family's lines below carry. The registration below predates the
#   lockset: the second wave made it on 2026-09-07 by the shape rule, while this paragraph still
#   held, and it was unearned until 2026-09-25. The corpus pair separates on the key; the idiom
#   lane separates on the lock (idiom_synchronizedCheckThenAct_onAConcurrentHashMap silent,
#   idiom_synchronizedCheckThenAct_withoutTheMonitor firing), as do the detector's unit tests.
#   What neither reaches: a lock the library never saw, which leaves the finding standing as it
#   does for every lockset detector, and a check-then-act whose every caller puts the same value,
#   which loses nothing and is still reported when recorded without the value. Since #827 a caller
#   can pass it, and a site whose every caller put the same instance is silent.
#
# Blank lines and # comments are ignored.

SHARED_JSON_MAPPER_RECONFIG = recorded_objectMapper_reconfigureWhileWriting, recorded_objectMapper_configuredThenShared
SHARED_MESSAGE_DIGEST = recorded_messageDigest_sharedAcrossThreads, recorded_messageDigest_guardedByItsOwnMonitor
SHARED_STATEFUL_CRYPTO = recorded_mac_sharedAcrossThreads, recorded_mac_confinedToOneThreadEach
SHARED_ITERATOR = recorded_concurrentHashMultiset_sharedIterator, recorded_concurrentHashMultiset_iteratorPerThread
JDBC_CONNECTION_SHARED = recorded_hoistedConnection_sharedAcrossThreads, recorded_hikariPool_checkoutPerThread
SHARED_BYTE_BUFFER = recorded_byteBuffer_relativeGetsShared, recorded_byteBuffer_absoluteGetsShared
WEAK_HASH_MAP_SHARED = recorded_weakHashMap_sharedAcrossThreads, recorded_weakHashMap_guardedByItsOwnMonitor

# --- Second wave, 2026-09-07.
#
# The lines above were registered when the recording lane held twelve pairs. The lane grew
# to 129 and none of the new pairs was ever registered, because promotion is a manual step
# and nothing noticed a pair that skipped it: the library's gate asks whether a VERDICT has
# evidence, never whether evidence has a VERDICT. So these sat at PROMPT holding a
# measurement that already met the bar.
#
# EveryEligiblePairIsPromotedOrExplainedTest now derives eligibility from the rows and fails
# until a qualifying pair is registered here, so the backlog cannot rebuild. Eligible means
# the detector is at PROMPT, both halves name the same class, and - in the recording lane -
# both reach the detector through the same record*/register* methods, so what separates them
# is the state the calls carry. Agent-lane bodies make no such calls; AgentRowPremise holds
# them to the same property instead.
# VISIBILITY was registered here until 1.12.3 and is PROMPT now. Its pair varies whether threads
# recorded different values for one field, and a correct AtomicInteger counter does exactly that:
# the detector records a name and a value, no write, lock or ordering, so no pair of its can tell a
# stale read from a value that is meant to change. It went to FACT first; the evidence caps below
# then took it to PROMPT, because "two threads saw different values in one round" is a thread
# count with no lock or ordering behind it (CONTEXT_FREE). The pair still runs.
SEMAPHORE = agent_semaphore_permitNeverReturned, agent_semaphore_permitReturnedInFinally
COUNTDOWN_LATCH = agent_countDownLatch_awaitTimedOut, agent_countDownLatch_awaitSawItsCount
