# --- Third wave, 2026-09-14: the first pairs promoted by reading rather than by the rule.
#
# The shape rule in corpus-eval's PairEvidence held these back as calling different detector
# methods, and in both cases the rule was misreading the source, not the pair. It counted
# CorpusRecorder.recordCrash, which is the harness keeping a thrown exception, as a detector
# call; and it read `synchronized (monitor)` as a call to a helper named `synchronized`, whose
# "body" was then the first synchronized block anywhere in the lane. With both fixed, the two
# pairs are same-shape, and each was read against its detector before being registered here:
#
#   NOTIFY_WITHOUT_MONITOR decides with Thread.holdsLock at the attempt, which is the JVM's own
#   IllegalMonitorStateException rule, so a monitor held any other way (a synchronized method,
#   a reentrant hold, an outer frame) stays silent, and the firing half proves its premise by
#   really calling notifyAll outside the monitor once and recording what the JVM threw.
#
#   SHARED_CHARSET_CODER keeps the same per-instance lockset, and has the same limits, as
#   SHARED_DEFLATER and SHARED_CHECKSUM above, on a pair of the same kind: one coder for every
#   thread against one per thread.
#
# The same reading held nine pairs back on their detector's model; PairEvidence.HELD_ON_MODEL
# carries each reason.
NOTIFY_WITHOUT_MONITOR = recorded_notify_withoutHoldingTheMonitor, recorded_notify_holdingTheMonitor
SHARED_CHARSET_CODER = recorded_charsetEncoder_sharedAcrossThreads, recorded_charsetEncoder_encoderPerThread

# --- 2026-09-14, #566: held on its model in the third wave, promoted once the model was fixed.
#
# LOCK_UPGRADE_DEADLOCK used to decide from the body's records alone: a write re-acquire by a
# thread already holding the write lock, which ReentrantReadWriteLock allows, was reported as a
# permanent deadlock, and read holds were a set, so read-twice-release-once went silent. It now
# asks the lock whenever the recording thread really holds it (isWriteLockedByCurrentThread and
# getReadHoldCount, both exact current-thread queries), and counts recorded read holds otherwise.
# Both corpus bodies take the real lock, and the silent half's write acquire really returns, so
# the pair is decided by the JDK's own rule. LockUpgradeDeadlockAccuracyTest pins both directions.

# --- 2026-09-17: held on its model in the second reading (#571), promoted once the pair was re-read.
#
# REENTRANT_LOCK used to report a recorded tryLock timeout. #589 made the finding a lock still held
# when the run is analysed, asked of the lock itself, with a timeout kept only as context; #609
# reports that hold only when its holder has finished or sits idle in its pool, and #608 reports
# starvation only when barging was seen on the lock. The firing half re-enters the real lock and
# releases it once, so a hold really is left taken. The silent half has every worker take a second
# lock with lock() and release it, contended but never left held. The halves also differ in the
# recorded timeout, which decides nothing; PairEvidence.REVIEWED_DESPITE_SHAPE records that reading.
#
# What the pair does not reach: the starvation finding, which needs the caller's
# recordStarvation(lock, ...) as well as barging seen on the lock, and the boundary the detector's
# javadoc names, a lock held by an unrecorded virtual thread still working at analysis, which is
# reported as if its holder had finished.
#
# The same re-read kept CYCLIC_BARRIER and CONDITION_VARIABLES at PROMPT on their model;
# PairEvidence.HELD_ON_MODEL carries each reason.
REENTRANT_LOCK = recorded_reentrantLock_holdLeftTaken, recorded_reentrantLock_acquiredAndReleased

# --- 2026-09-19, #665: held on its model since the second reading, promoted once the model changed.
#
# CYCLIC_BARRIER reported one arrival at a broken barrier, so a late party that catches
# BrokenBarrierException and drops a barrier broken to cancel it drew the reuse finding. Reuse is
# now a party (the recording thread) coming back to a barrier it already saw broken, asked of the
# barrier's isBroken() at each arrival, with no reset in between; a reset is recorded, or observed
# when a later arrival finds the barrier whole. Both halves below make the same three calls
# (registerBarrier, recordAwait, recordBroken) on a really broken barrier and differ only in whether
# the party comes back to it. The lane also holds the handled-break twin (#662) and the stranded
# pair, untimed against timed await (#631). CyclicBarrierDetectorAccuracyTest and
# DetectorAccuracyEvalTest pin both directions.
#
# What the pair does not reach: a barrier shared across rounds on fresh virtual threads, where no
# party comes back and the reuse is missed, and a reset nobody recorded with no recorded arrival
# while the barrier was whole, after which the party's next broken arrival is reported.
CYCLIC_BARRIER = recorded_cyclicBarrier_awaitedWhileBroken, recorded_cyclicBarrier_cancelledAndDropped

# --- 2026-09-19, #666: held on its model since the second reading, promoted once the model changed.
#
# CONDITION_VARIABLES had three findings decided from the body's records or the lock alone: a
# thread parked on a condition registered with its lock but no predicate (an idle consumer parks the
# same way), a recorded await with no exit on a condition registered without its lock, and a missing
# signal, a recordAwaitExit(..., false) with no recordSignal. All three are notes now. The one
# finding left is a thread the lock's getWaitQueueLength shows parked while the predicate registered
# with registerCondition(lock, condition, ready, name) holds, with no thread queued to re-acquire the
# lock (#657). Both halves below start the same textbook consumer loop through one helper, register
# the same way and make the same calls; they differ only in whether work arrived on the queue while
# the threads signalled a different condition. ConditionVariableDetectorLockAndRoundsTest and
# DetectorAccuracyEvalTest pin both directions.
#
# What the pair does not reach: a stuck waiter behind unrelated contention on the lock at analysis,
# which is noted rather than reported (#657), and a predicate that is wrong about what the waiter
# waits for, which the detector evaluates but cannot check.
CONDITION_VARIABLES = recorded_condition_awaitedWithNoSignal, recorded_condition_consumerIdleOnAnEmptyQueue

# --- 2026-09-26, #819: held on its model since #755, promoted once the model changed.
#
# FILE_CHANNEL_POSITION_RACE judged single accesses, so threads that each made one self-contained
# read(buffer) or write(buffer) drew the finding, and FileChannel runs one operation involving the
# position at a time, so those lose nothing: a probe (8 threads, 5,000 operations each, JDK 21 and
# 26) read every chunk once and wrote every record whole. The finding is now a position(n)-then-I/O
# sequence on one thread with another thread's implicit-position call that no common lock and no
# happens-before edge keeps out of it, the shape the same probe read wrong about 1,500 times in
# 40,000. Both halves below seek and read the same shared channel through the same calls and
# differ only in synchronized (channel). The lane also holds the self-contained reads that were the
# firing row until #819, now silent, and the positional-read twin, which calls
# recordPositionalAccess and decides nothing; PairEvidence.REVIEWED_DESPITE_SHAPE records that
# reading. FileChannelPositionRaceDetectorTest pins both directions.
#
# What the pair does not reach: a lock released and taken again between the seek and the I/O,
# which reads as held across and is not reported, and a self-contained call that relies on where
# an earlier one left the cursor, such as write(buffer) then position(), which is no sequence.
FILE_CHANNEL_POSITION_RACE = recorded_fileChannel_seekThenReadShared, recorded_fileChannel_seekThenReadUnderItsOwnMonitor

